From 46e654f907b95c809e45b3320bdfec9ce521811a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karthik Singaravadivelan <karthik@axelrod-ai.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:18:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] World model service tools in the MCP catalog: read only (the
 service's v1 API)

The world_model_* tools read the Axelrod world model service's v1 API (/v1/world-models/{id}/...) for the signed-in
org user's organization: world models and versions pinned reads, entities and attributes, the taxonomy, search, a
company's construction and traces (through totals, to a depth), simulations, the v4.1.4 export, documents, bundles and
proposed changes. Each tool takes a world_model_id (default: the organization's only world model).

Read only, as agreed in the API review (Oct 19): core's backend MCP does not ingest, propose, simulate or decide.
Writes reach the world model through its web interface and the data-ingestion pipeline. The organization's key holds
world_model:read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
